   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I am trying to overlay a maximum credibility clade over\r\n a sample of the trees in the posterior (produced by beast), e.g.:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">trees </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rcoal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Example sample of posterior trees.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;multiPhylo&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tree </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rcoal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Maximum credibility tree.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;rectangular&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;skyblue&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\"><br></span></div><div>However,\r\n when plotting this, all the roots line up, whereas in reality, it is \r\nthe tips that should line up (because these are sampled at a specific \r\npoint in time). I know I can use the <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">mrsd</span> setting in <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">ggtree()</span>, but then I cannot do the same with <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">geom_tree()</span>,\r\n which then plots the two in very different points of the axis, e.g.:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><code><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;rectangular&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;skyblue&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">, mrsd=as.Date(&#39;2010-01-01&#39;))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></code><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone\r\nknow how I could get by this problem, or alternatively right align the \r\ntrees being plotted?</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
