     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, October 16, 2018 at 11:36:14 PM UTC-4, Yu, Guangchuang wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:0px 0px 1.2em!important\">I think <a href=\"https://twitter.com/willgearty/status/1050458320543330305\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://twitter.com/willgearty/status/1050458320543330305&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482441929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2-BgTMQ6CdOp_ltmQLkweN\">this tweet</a> is helpful to your question.</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdiBkaXI9Imx0ciI+SSB0aGluayBbdGhpcyB0d2VldF0oaHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS93\r\naWxsZ2VhcnR5L3N0YXR1cy8xMDUwNDU4MzIwNTQzMzMwMzA1KSBpcyBoZWxwZnVsIHRvIHlvdXIg\r\ncXVlc3Rpb24uPGJyPjwvZGl2Pg==\" style=\"min-height:0;width:0;max-height:0;max-width:0;overflow:hidden;font-size:0em;padding:0;margin:0\"></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Tue, Oct 16, 2018 at 9:51 PM &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">bgarcia...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hi,</div><div><br></div><div>I am trying to overlay a maximum credibility clade over\r\n a sample of the trees in the posterior (produced by beast), e.g.:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">trees </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> lapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rcoal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Example sample of posterior trees.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;multiPhylo&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tree </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rcoal</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">50</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">                    </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># Maximum credibility tree.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;rectangular&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;skyblue&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div></div><div><span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\"><br></span></div><div>However,\r\n when plotting this, all the roots line up, whereas in reality, it is \r\nthe tips that should line up (because these are sampled at a specific \r\npoint in time). I know I can use the <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">mrsd</span> setting in <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">ggtree()</span>, but then I cannot do the same with <span style=\"font-family:monospace,monospace\">geom_tree()</span>,\r\n which then plots the two in very different points of the axis, e.g.:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><code><span style=\"color:#000\">p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trees</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> layout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;rectangular&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> color</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;skyblue&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> alpha</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">, mrsd=as.Date(&#39;2010-01-01&#39;))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> theme_tree2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></code><span style=\"color:#660\"></span></div></code></div></div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone\r\nknow how I could get by this problem, or alternatively right align the \r\ntrees being plotted?</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nG Yu, DK Smith, H Zhu, Y Guan, TTY Lam*. ggtree: an R package for visualization and annotation of phylogenetic trees with their covariates and other associated data, Methods in Ecology and Evolution, 2017, 8(1):28-36. doi:10.1111/2041-210X.12628<br>\r\n <br>\r\nHomepage: <a href=\"https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482441929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Clxtq_TRXjlFMAjx9_tQU\">https://guangchuangyu.github.io/software/ggtree</a><br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;ggtree&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-ggtree...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">bioc-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/56a8374c-e03d-4400-a298-204def836d5f%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/56a8374c-e03d-4400-a298-204def836d5f%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482441929000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0cP8yPQ2gsTn3yrUedzygC\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/bioc-ggtree/56a8374c-e03d-4400-a298-204def836d5f%40googlegroups.com</a